/-!
# A general 8-byte `growslice` stub for `GrowsliceLiveContract` (arm64), any request

Shared witness stub (agent top). Janus's `LiveStubGrow` serves one pinned request (closed numerals); `RunIface.Serves`
asks the runtime to serve every `growslice` of `[]Word` up to `2^17` elements, so the witness runtime needs a stub that
computes Go's growth rule for every request: `grCode` (generated by `scripts/gen-grow-stub.py`, 242 words, position
independent: `RelocArm64.CodeOK`):

* `nextslicecap(newLen, oldCap)` (`runtime/slice.go`; Janus `Alloc.nextslicecap`): `newLen` when `newLen > 2·oldCap`,
  `2·oldCap` when `oldCap < 256`, else the loop `c += (c + 768) / 4` until `c ≥ newLen`;
* `roundupsize(8·c, noscan)` (Janus `Alloc.roundupsize`): a compare chain over the 67 size classes for `8·c ≤ 32760`,
  page rounding `(size + 8191) / 8192 · 8192` above;
* the toy bump allocation of `A = 16 K` bytes, the byte copy of the `8·(newLen - num)` old bytes, and the result
  `(p, newLen, K / 8)`.

The stub is proved at `E0 = 2^48` and moved to any address by `RelocArm64.summary_transport` (`growslice_live_at`).
-/

